'''Sentry''' is an [[Elite]] found in [[Act 1]] in groups of three. In [[Act 2]], a Sentry can be fought as a common [[Slay the Spire Wiki/Enemies|Enemy]].
== Pattern ==
{{Intents|Sentry}}
Uses {{Int|Sentry|Bolt}} followed by {{Int|Sentry|Beam}}, repeating for the rest of the combat.

In the Elite encounter, the middle '''Sentry''' instead uses {{Int|Sentry|Beam}} followed by {{Int|Sentry|Bolt}}.

== In Party With ==

=== Act 1 ===
As an [[Elite]] alongside:

* 2 other '''Sentries'''

=== Act 2 ===
In the hard pool alongside:

* 1 {{M|Spheric Guardian}}

== Hints ==
* During the Elite encounter, you should focus in eliminating the 1st or the 3rd '''Sentry''' as fast as possible, ignoring the 2nd one. This prevents you from taking 18 ({{Asc|3|20}}) damage each other turn, making the rest of the fight much easier.

* The {{C|Dazed}} in your discard pile won't hamper you as long as you have cards remaining in your draw pile. Once you run out of cards, they will be shuffled into your draw pile and massively reduce your ability to draw playable cards. It is important to kill at least one of the Sentries ''before'' you shuffle your draw pile, as you may no longer have the ability to deal with all '''Sentries''' at the same time once the {{C|Dazed}} come in.

* {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Evolve}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}} and {{C|Fire Breathing}} convert {{C|Dazed}} into advantage.

== Trivia ==
* Sentry appears in the artwork of {{C|Searing Blow}}, {{C|Reaper}}, {{C|Predator}}, {{C|Reflex}}, {{C|Malaise}}, {{C|Fear No Evil}} and {{C|Rushdown}}.

